WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.810
Yeah, I'm almost home.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.200
We'll discuss this issue at tomorrow's meeting.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.020
President Kazamori?!

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.450
Even if that's his title, this company still belongs to the Sasa family.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.520
There's no need to obey everything he says.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.640
Kazamori, it's not like that!

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.870
I wasn't trying to leave you out and make the decisions myself.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:08.730
Can I pay you a visit?

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.260
Kigihiko-san, we're starting our prayer session soon.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.140
N-Nee-san... I was going to see Kazamori...

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.870
He won't come anyway.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.240
Let's go, Fumihiko.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.140
Okay...

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:36.060
Komamori-sama, Komamori-sama,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.600
please protect and watch over us.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.450
Please protect the Sasa family.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:44.840
Today marks seven years since your untimely death.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:48.040
The Sasa family has continued to thrive.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.630
Komamori-sama, Komamori-sama,

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.920
Komamori-sama, Komamori-sama.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:52.920
Nee-san?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.170
I'll call my brother to join us.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.170
Brother? Do you mean Kazamori-san?

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:02.430
It's enough that we, his true blood relatives, are in attendance.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.060
Even if he was adopted, Kazamori nii-sama is the head of this family.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.060
He should at least be with us on the anniversary of his father's death.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.900
That guy loves being closed off, all by himself, nee-san.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.980
Mitsuko!

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:20.700
I've told you already,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.860
Kazamori-san is afflicted by illness,
so you must keep your distance from him.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.870
Komamori-sama, Komamori-sama,

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.300
Fumihiko, one of your blood,

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.820
will be graduating university without issue and will be entering the business in spring.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.380
A blackout?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.340
Kazamori nii-sama?

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:02.160
I'm so glad... I thought something might have happened to you.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.030
Um... You haven't shown me your face for quite some time...

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.560
Kazamori-kun!

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.040
Come back inside, quickly!

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.440
Kazamori!

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.700
Hey! Did something happen?!

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.440
Kazamori!

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.340
Nee-san.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.440
Kazamori!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.450
It's just like seven years ago, today...

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:45.950
Kazamori!

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.410
Taku-sensei... what is this?

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.870
Kazamori-kun...

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.010
Kazamori?

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:00.590
No way...

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:05.070
Kazamori... by the time I took notice, he was already ablaze!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:05.760
Micchan!

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:14.810
There's no way that could be Kazamori-kun... That's too...

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.810
Kazamori-san! Kazamori-san!

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.680
It's a curse...

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.950
You're right! This is my husband's curse!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.030
I see... this is the anniversary of my brother's death...

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:32.330
A curse, huh?

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:35.710
That can't be...

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.250
Sign: Shinjuku Station, East

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:04.650
Hello, restricted area admittance guards. You're doing a fine job!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.740
What happened? An explosion?!

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.370
Are we okay?

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:13.950
Ah... no, no, no!

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.000
Lethal force in response to terrorist attacks has been authorised.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.590
A reformation of the Regulations for
Self-Defence Forces was passed today,

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.710
receiving unanimous approval from
members of the House of Representatives.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:31.470
Currently, emergency procedures are
scheduled to occur three days from now.

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:35.060
In accordance, all forces participating in
observational responsibilities overseas...

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.410
...will be eligible for reassignment to combat duty.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:27.610
You're so rough! Do it to me gently!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.360
Shinjuurou!

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:37.740
Hey!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.740
Please, don't go!

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:45.880
I'm sorry...

00:07:58.530 --> 00:07:59.590
It's like it won't connect...

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:02.730
...or rather, the connection is being rejected.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.070
Shinjuurou!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.570
Take a look!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:11.900
It's talks!

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:16.030
Shovel: Scoops and shovels are opposites sizes in Kansai.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:18.110
Wow!

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.870
TL Note: Inga says "shaberu", which means to speak, but also sounds like a word for shovel.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:20.380
It's just picking up vocabulary off the net using...

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.860
...the kind of chip you find in old game consoles.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:23.980
Do you not have any others to try?

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:27.630
All of my customers have the mail address for that phone.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.730
Customers... you mean your...

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:32.050
You know.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:35.180
Don't tell me you negotiate price through texts as well...

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:39.230
Well, if he's nice, I'll try to give him a discount!

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:42.820
The contents of all messages are code-checked;

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:46.280
possible terrorist activities and other illegal dealings are identified...

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.440
...and the perpetrators have their access cut.

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.490
Do something about it, Detective-san!

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.150
You're acquainted with Chairman Kaishou, aren't you?

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.720
He's "The Defeated Detective"!

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.660
He's currently building record losses against Chairman Kaishou!

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:01.900
That man holds the communications network in one hand,

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:04.730
and is the advisor on all military and police analysis.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.000
He's quite the elite.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:10.780
But at this rate I'll lose all of my customers!

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:15.100
Shinjuurou! Horses!

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.560
Yuuki Shinjuurou!

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.360
I have a case that I want to consult you on!

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.900
Seems troublesome...

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:24.810
I'm gonna make myself disappear.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.890
Have you forgotten me? It's Rie!

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.210
Kaishou Rie!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.270
Kaishou...?

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:30.990
Is she...?

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.020
I have one condition.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.930
I'd like your dad to use his connections to reconnect a smart phone.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:03.890
Huh?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.760
Why horses?

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.050
I was told that your residence is within the restricted entry zone.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:15.570
What?

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:20.560
There's an ordinance deeming that no one can enter by car or foot,

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.780
but there wasn't anything about entering on a horse.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.910
That's a first-class brain you've got.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.930
I'm Kaishou Rinroku's daughter.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.880
I can't break the law.

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:30.790
You...

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.350
What's your name?

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:34.290
Inga!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:37.550
Inga...? Isn't Inga...?

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.970
You're that woman's little brother?

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:54.400
This here is the younger sister of the late Sasa Kazamori, Mitsuko-san.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:59.540
She contacted my father right away following an incident last night.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:05.030
I wanted Chairman Kaishou to prove that my brother wasn't killed by a curse.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:06.450
A curse?!

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:07.950
Yes...

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.240
It's a curse...

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:14.670
Who would be putting a curse on you?

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:18.410
They think it's my father's curse...

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.780
Might you know of my father, Sasa Komamori?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.430
Sure don't!

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:26.050
Uh, I'm not too familiar with him either.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.270
Even though he was all over the news?

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.270
I wasn't in this country at the time.

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:38.440
Sasa Komamori was a researcher of artificial intelligence.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.280
To create machines with intellect equal to humans,

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:45.020
which could even pass the Turing Test,

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.930
and sell them as entertainment products...

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.940
...Sasa Komamori was truly a genius.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:53.330
I heard something about him being a weirdo who
always donned a mask when in the presence of others.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:57.640
He said it was to hide his embarrassment when meeting people,

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:00.090
but I always assumed he was trying to build an image for himself.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:04.090
But seven years after Komamori-san died in that manner,

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.240
Kazamori-kun also...

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:10.350
I do know about R.A.I.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:13.590
A program that can mimic human thought processes.

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:16.480
There were even exclusive bodies
created for them as well, weren't there?

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:21.860
But my father's inventions became illegal under new legislation.

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:26.240
In the middle of the war, a search team of police was deployed.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.190
Sasa Komamori, we have suspicion...

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:32.750
...that your research is in considerable violation of the New Information Privacy Protection Act.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:34.380
Mother...

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:37.250
This entire country has gone insane.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.120
Just how much has that man, Sasa Komamori,

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.380
contributed to this world?

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.890
Kazamori nii-sama?

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.270
Is father with you?

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.240
Father!

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:08.410
An explosion!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.240
Ow...

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:13.350
After the remains of my father were verified,

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:18.750
the remaining fortune and related business
responsibilities were passed on to Kazamori nii-sama.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:22.250
Why would nii-sama receive this curse from Komamori-shi?

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:28.640
Kazamori onii-sama was suddenly brought to our house one day.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.430
Father said that he was the child of a distant relative...

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:36.600
...but also that he had adopted him and would be naming him successor.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.810
He named his adopted son as his heir?

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:42.810
As proof of his successorship, he started wearing one of those masks from the very beginning.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:45.610
Mask!

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:54.120
Therefore, I have never witnessed his true face...

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.250
...and now I'll never be able to see it.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.500
On the anniversary of Sasa Komamori's death,

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.500
the successor is engulfed in flames, meeting the same end.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.180
Makes you think it's a curse, doesn't it, Detective-san?

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.420
This is my uncle, Kigihiko.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:18.110
Kazamori never showed his face at the
company and was president in name only.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.440
The entire group was run by my sister and me.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:25.190
Nii-sama only came to avoid people so desperately because of that mask.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.320
He still made decisions on all the most important issues.

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.000
Fumihiko, what are you doing?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.250
Now that Kazamori is no longer among us,

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.670
Fumihiko has become the new head of this household.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.630
On a separate note, I don't care if you're the daughter of Chairman Kaishou;

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.490
for you to bring a detective along with you is an insult to us.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:56.060
Well then, do you really think that a curse exists?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.810
Of course that was just a figure of speech.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.890
Kazamori suffered shock from the death of my husband...

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:05.120
...and was afflicted by an emotional imbalance.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.650
Enough so that he constantly needed his doctor, Taku-sensei, by his side.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.230
Where is this Taku-sensei?

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:13.910
The doctor is resting, due to the burns he sustained.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:20.860
My husband's death caused Kazamori-san constant anguish, just like a curse.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:25.130
When he reached his breaking point, he simply chose to die the same way as my husband.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.170
No.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.920
Kazamori nii-sama wouldn't ever commit suicide.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:30.170
Why is that?

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.930
Nii-sama knew something.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.550
He was trying to warn us that some kind of danger was near.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.270
Just like seven years ago...

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:45.360
He was already prepared to commit suicide and was telling you to stay away, Micchan.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.110
No!

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.360
Izumi-chan, huh?

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:56.120
And just why are you two here?

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.810
I requested that he be here...

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:01.120
...once I heard that you were going to leave the deduction to my father.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:04.070
Chairman Kaishou is going to examine this?

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:07.880
They say he can solve any puzzle
without even appearing on the scene...

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:14.210
If my father is trying to make another lie in order to protect "something bigger"...

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:15.890
...I won't allow it.

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:16.890
Don't worry.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.030
I'll tell you the deduction that the Chairman reached.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.140
This way.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:27.820
Other than his mask, Kazamori-kun was an intellectual and composed executive.

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:31.260
For him to become obsessed with his father's death and commit suicide is unthinkable.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.740
However, there are cases where people take such actions on impulse.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:37.780
Then why didn't he mimic it entirely, explosion and all?

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:42.460
I sense a scheme to link Kazamori-kun and Komamori-shi's deaths.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.790
This was a murder.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.810
A murder?!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.290
Apart from the victim, there were five individuals present.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:53.430
The victim's stepmother, Sasa Itoji-san.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:56.480
The victim's uncle, Sasa Kigihiko-san.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:00.480
The victim's step-siblings, Mitsuko-san and Fumihiko-san.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.810
And finally, Dr. Taku Hidenobu.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:06.750
Whoa, nee-san and I are both suspects!

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:11.510
We can say that Fumihiko, who stood to succeed the company and become the head of household,

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:16.860
had the most to gain in the event of Kazamori-shi's death.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.700
No.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:21.510
Fumihiko left the room after I did.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:25.710
Chairman Kaishou has also said that he can't imagine Fumihiko was involved.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:30.430
There was a time when Sasa Kigihiko-shi assisted Komamori-shi,

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:32.430
and he's knowledgeable about mechanical engineering.

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:34.620
It would be a simple matter for him to tamper with a cable in the room,

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:37.820
setting it to catch fire at a specific time.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:42.140
But even with Kazamori-shi dead, Kigihiko wouldn't stand to inherit anything...

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:45.350
Who's the one who wants Fumihiko to succeed the company most?

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:48.730
The mother.

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:57.100
You're saying I asked Kigihiko to murder him for Fumihiko's sake?

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:57.740
How rude!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.400
What's your interpretation of it?

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:03.490
Hey!

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:05.520
Help us out here!

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.370
We had no reason to kill Kazamori!

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.080
There's no way we could have!

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.130
Kigihiko-san!

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:12.500
No way you... could have?

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:14.770
We'll have to tell him, nee-san...

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:16.060
At this rate, we'll be...

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:17.900
We'll continue this in the interrogation room.

00:18:24.190 --> 00:18:25.770
It's a surveillance camera.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:27.910
That's it!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.030
This must mean that Kazamori put
surveillance cameras all over the house...

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.520
...and was watching every move we made.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:34.020
If that's the case...

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:36.360
Wait!

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.840
Shinjuurou...

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:56.590
My spirit is swirling...

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.220
I've waited long enough, right?

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:00.680
Wait, Inga!

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:02.930
I can't hold it in!

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.570
Come now...

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:24.070
What should I ask... and to whom?

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.800
It's all recorded!

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:41.210
No matter how far back you search,
you won't find me sabotaging anything.

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:42.590
Check it yourself!

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:45.570
That's why I said it was suicide!

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.600
I wonder about that...

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:00.570
That woman again...

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.700
Just who are you?

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.820
She's my boss.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:08.020
She said she has something to ask, or whatever.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.960
A built-in computer, huh?

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.460
Tell me...

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:18.710
Who is Sasa Kazamori?

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:22.590
Who is he under that mask?

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:26.460
Someone was posing as Kazamori?

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:27.850
You don't have to answer that!

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:29.500
It's hopeless to resist.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:33.420
People have no choice but to answer what she asks.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:34.480
Just one question...

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:39.190
Who is... Sasa Kazamori?

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:41.740
Who?

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.570
Who?

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:02.880
He doesn't exist...

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.000
Mother!

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:07.760
There never was a human by the name of Kazamori!

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.140
That means...

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:12.970
Kazamori wasn't human.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:16.060
Isn't that right, Kazamori-san?

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:37.500
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:45.460
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:53.140
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:57.520
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:01.480
We follow it along.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:05.440
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:09.450
Like a falling feather.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:12.580
Looking for, find it,

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:18.910
So we can come closer together.

00:22:33.430 --> 00:22:37.430
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:37.430 --> 00:22:41.440
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:44.520
Looking for, find it,

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:49.360
So we can come closer together.

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:54.830
The original work for next time is the
same as this time, "Masked Mansion".

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:56.170
But that's not all...

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:58.830
A story called "Shoplifting Family" is in there too?

00:22:58.830 --> 00:23:00.540
I'll give it a read!

00:23:00.540 --> 00:23:01.620
Huh?

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:07.160
It's like in this old family, there are all these members and
people connected to them, and everyone has a hidden secret.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:08.800
This story is kind of similar to ours.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:15.010
Don't tell me Ango-sensei has gone through all this trouble so he can blow the whistle on sharing ideas!

00:23:15.010 --> 00:23:17.470
I like that kind of meanness!

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:19.390
So anyway, next time on UN-GO:

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:20.680
"An Unmasked Residence!"
